 ## The desk
 
 The window is one symmetrical desk: two graphite bands, the head at the top and the writing line at the bottom, with warm paper between them, a pane at each side and your work in the centre. Both panes are one width (drag either edge and both follow; Settings → Workspace → Left column width sets both), and the desk is mirrored about the window's centre to the pixel. Lettering on the bands is pale, as if erased from the shading; words you can act on are eraser pink; the choice in use has a short yellow mark under it. Words you may skip (a caption, a note, an explanation) are in the script, and what you act on or read first stays in print. The desk's measures are in docs/GRAPHITE_DESK.md, and its "Where things went" says where each older control went.
 
